{
  "description": "#6206 — `list_distinct_unfit_property_values` groups a key's values that don't fit it by the value as shown (the text `5` and a peer's number 5 are one), with live and Trash counts, paged by that value in byte order. `convert_unfit_property_values` replaces each mapped value, the Trash's included, by its replacement read under the key's type, as one `rewrite_properties` op (reason `convert_unfit`); a value left out stays. It is refused when a mapped value's counts are stale (`UnacknowledgedPropertyLoss`) and when a replacement doesn't fit: a date that is no calendar day, blank text, a select value outside the options. `undo_ops` puts the values back, still not fitting, and `redo_page_op` converts them again. With nothing held under a mapped value it appends no op. A peer's number and boolean under a text key and under a select with options convert to a text and to options. One replacement of the `5` converts the text and the number, and `undo_ops` gives each back in its own form. `whenx` changes from text to date: `X`'s date fits; the trashed `Y`'s \"never\", `Z`'s and `W`'s \"soon\", the trashed `V`'s \"later\", `U`'s peer number 5 and `T`'s \"5\" do not. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
